# Ledger

Research-first Python toolkit for a long-only liquid equity sleeve: compare strategy families on one sample, apply an explicit change bar, then propose holdings moves with reasons.

**Not regulated financial advice.** Past performance is not future returns.

Public demo (scrubbed KPIs + history): [orbit-rho-rouge.vercel.app/ledger-research](https://orbit-rho-rouge.vercel.app/ledger-research)  
Case study: [Ledger research cycle](https://orbit-rho-rouge.vercel.app/writes/ledger-research-cycle-strategy-selection)

## What it does

```powershell
invest research --open
```

1. Backtests candidate families (ETF buy&hold opportunity cost, universe EW, momentum variants).
2. Selects a **run** policy under documented rules (Sharpe rank, turnover tie-break, change bar).
3. Compares current holdings to that policy and writes explained EXIT / ADD / TRIM / DEFER actions.
4. Publishes a **public** snapshot under `dashboard/research/` (no broker names, no absolute € amounts).
5. Copies that scrub into Orbit `public/ledger-research` (`invest publish-orbit`) so [alextouvras.com/ledger-research](https://alextouvras.com/ledger-research) updates after a Slack holdings run.

Also: `invest sim`, `invest review`, `invest validate`, `invest compare`, `invest calendar`, `invest catalog-gate`, `invest holdings`.

## Cadence

| When | What |
|------|------|
| **Mar / Sep** (~1 month before) | `invest catalog-gate` — review research vs strategy catalog; human approves any CANDIDATES / policy tweaks |
| **Apr / Oct** | Slack holdings → `invest research` → you approve trades |
